---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const [profile] = await getCollection('profile');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Both Sides of the Discount Moved — Braeden Keena"
  description="A 9,077-facility longitudinal pricing study (as of 15 September 2026). Daily exact-listing snapshots show reference rates rising a median of $45 on the same day 40%-off promotions were assigned."
>
  <Nav name={profile.data.name} />

  <article class="study-page">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <header class="study-header">
        <div class="study-kicker-row">
          <span class="study-kicker">Storage Price Observatory · Longitudinal Pricing Investigation</span>
          <span class="study-badge">9,077 Facilities · 129,704 Daily SKUs (15 Sept 2026)</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="study-title">Both Sides of the Discount Moved.</h1>
        <p class="study-provenance">
          A finding from the <strong>Storage Price Observatory</strong>. A single baseline snapshot
          of Public Storage was taken 29 April 2026; continuous daily collection began 9 July 2026.
          The six other collections were added during September
          2026. Through 25 August that Public Storage collection was published as a directory called <a href="/work/findstorage">FindStorage</a> — a product since retired, whose headline
          figures are frozen at that date and reported separately from the figures here.
        </p>
        <p class="study-lede">
          A percentage-off advertisement contains two numbers: the stated discount and the baseline rate used to calculate savings. 
          When daily snapshots followed exact listings through time, both numbers moved together:
          reference rates rose by a median of $45 on the same day "40% off" discounts appeared, and when rates were later cut, roughly half the promotional value was withdrawn alongside them — leaving modeled four-month cost slightly higher than before.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Top Hard Stats Grid -->
      <div class="stat-banner">
        <!-- Event 1: 1 August Reference-Rate Hike -->
        <div class="stat-group">
          <div class="stat-group__header">
            <span class="stat-group__tag">1 August</span>
            <span class="stat-group__title">Reference-rate increase assigned with promotion</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-group__cards">
            <div class="stat-banner__card">
              <span class="stat-banner__num">4,904 / 4,904</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">1 August listings entering the promo that also received a rate hike</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__sub">0 / 428 in 28 July control (0.0%)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-banner__card">
              <span class="stat-banner__num text-alert">+$45</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">median reference-rate increase, same day the 40%-off was assigned</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Event 2: 14 September Portfolio Reset -->
        <div class="stat-group stat-group--conclusion">
          <div class="stat-group__header">
            <span class="stat-group__tag">14 September</span>
            <span class="stat-group__title">Headline rate cut and promotional withdrawal</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-group__cards">
            <div class="stat-banner__card">
              <span class="stat-banner__num">−14.7%</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">rates fell, across 59,045 exact-matched modelable listings, 14 Sept</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-banner__card stat-banner__card--featured">
              <span class="stat-banner__tag">The Net Outcome</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__num text-alert">+1.1%</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__lbl">modeled four-month cost to the customer — higher, despite the rate cut</span>
              <span class="stat-banner__sub">promotional discount value withdrawn: −49.7%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- VISUAL 1: the 28 July control against the 1 August event -->
      <section class="visual-card">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <span class="visual-card__eyebrow">The Smoking Gun · Physical Control</span>
          <h2>The Control That Rules Out a System Glitch</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            Could a website update engine simply bundle rate and promo updates together? 
            July supplies the empirical control. Four days before August 1, hundreds of listings rotated into the same discount with zero rate hikes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-grid">
          <!-- July 28 Control -->
          <div class="evidence-panel">
            <div class="evidence-panel__top">
              <span class="evidence-date">July 28, 2026</span>
              <span class="evidence-tag">The Control</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-stat">
              <strong>0 / 428</strong>
              <span>promo entrants received a rate increase (0.0%)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-bar-track">
              <div class="evidence-bar-fill" style="width: 0%;"></div>
            </div>
            <p class="evidence-note">
              428 listings entered "40% off For 4 Months". Rates remained completely flat. Proves rate and promo fields are independently writable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- August 1 Event -->
          <div class="evidence-panel evidence-panel--alert">
            <div class="evidence-panel__top">
              <span class="evidence-date">August 1, 2026</span>
              <span class="evidence-tag evidence-tag--alert">The Coordinated Wave</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-stat">
              <strong class="text-alert">4,904 / 4,904</strong>
              <span>promo entrants received an immediate rate increase (100.0%)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="evidence-bar-track">
              <div class="evidence-bar-fill evidence-bar-fill--alert" style="width: 100%;"></div>
            </div>
            <p class="evidence-note text-alert">
              Every single listing entering the 4-month promo had its reference rate increased on the exact same morning. Median hike: +$45.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="evidence-aggregate" style="margin-top: 18px; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
          Measured on that same 4,904-offer event cohort, headline value rose 35.3% and promotional value rose 216.4%, producing a 2.1% reduction in aggregate modeled four-month cost — though the median offer cost $2 more, 55.8% of listings cost more over four months, and 96% cost more by month eight.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- VISUAL 2: Costa Mesa — how the advertised savings figure was calculated -->
      <section class="visual-card">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <span class="visual-card__eyebrow">Single-Unit Reconstruction</span>
          <h2>Anatomy of an Advertised "Savings" Figure</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            Costa Mesa facility #235, SKU V_1455679 — normalized as 5x15 in the feed, presented on the live page as 7.5x10. Daily snapshots show the reference rate at $161 on 20 August, raised to $237 on the 22nd, carrying a 40%-off offer on the 24th, and back to $161 on the 25th. Every rate and promotion below is reproducible from <code>history/rate_changes.csv</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Chart 1: the advertised reference rate, and which promotion was running -->
        <div class="chart-container">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 300" class="svg-chart" role="img" aria-label="Daily advertised reference rate for Costa Mesa store 235, 20 to 26 August 2026, showing $161 rising to $237 on 22 August and returning to $161 on 25 August">
            <line x1="80" y1="40" x2="770" y2="40" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="45" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$240</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="109" x2="770" y2="109" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="114" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$200</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="178" x2="770" y2="178" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="183" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$160</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="230" x2="770" y2="230" stroke="var(--border)" />
            <text x="65" y="235" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$130</text>

            <!-- 24 August: the day the 40%-off offer appeared -->
            <line x1="533" y1="40" x2="533" y2="230" stroke="rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.45)" stroke-dasharray="3" />

            <!-- Reference rate: 161, 161, 237, 237, 237, 161, 161 -->
            <path d="M 120 176 L 223 176 L 327 45 L 430 45 L 533 45 L 637 176 L 740 176" fill="none" stroke="#e05252" stroke-width="3" />
            <circle cx="120" cy="176" r="4" fill="#e05252" />
            <circle cx="223" cy="176" r="4" fill="#e05252" />
            <circle cx="327" cy="45" r="4" fill="#e05252" />
            <circle cx="430" cy="45" r="4" fill="#e05252" />
            <circle cx="533" cy="45" r="6" fill="#e05252" />
            <circle cx="637" cy="176" r="4" fill="#e05252" />
            <circle cx="740" cy="176" r="4" fill="#e05252" />

            <text x="430" y="32" fill="#e05252" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">$237 struck-through reference rate (+47%)</text>
            <text x="120" y="198" fill="#6bb0a8" font-size="11" font-weight="700">$161 — the rate on either side of the window</text>

            <!-- The only day the 40%-off price was actually offered -->
            <circle cx="533" cy="209" r="5" fill="var(--accent)" />
            <text x="521" y="213" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="end">$142.20 promotional rate (40% off $237)</text>

            <!-- Day labels -->
            <text x="120" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 20</text>
            <text x="223" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 21</text>
            <text x="327" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 22</text>
            <text x="430" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 23</text>
            <text x="533" y="250" fill="#d97706" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Aug 24</text>
            <text x="637" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 25</text>
            <text x="740" y="250" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 26</text>

            <!-- Which promotion was running, by segment -->
            <line x1="120" y1="268" x2="430" y2="268" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="275" y="285" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">promotion: $1 first month rent</text>
            <line x1="500" y1="268" x2="566" y2="268" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="533" y="285" fill="#d97706" font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">40% off, 4 months</text>
            <line x1="637" y1="268" x2="740" y2="268" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="688" y="285" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">2nd month free</text>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <!-- Chart 2: what four months of rent actually cost under each day's offer -->
        <div class="chart-container">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 268" class="svg-chart" role="img" aria-label="Four-month cost of the offer advertised each day: $484 on 20 and 21 August, $712 on the 22nd and 23rd, $568.80 on the 24th, $483 on the 25th and 26th">
            <text x="80" y="18" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12">Four months of rent under the offer on the page that day</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="30" x2="770" y2="30" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="34" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$800</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="75" x2="770" y2="75" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="79" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$600</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="120" x2="770" y2="120" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="124" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$400</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="165" x2="770" y2="165" stroke="var(--border-soft)" stroke-dasharray="4" />
            <text x="65" y="169" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$200</text>
            <line x1="80" y1="210" x2="770" y2="210" stroke="var(--border)" />
            <text x="65" y="214" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">$0</text>

            <rect x="90" y="101" width="60" height="109" fill="#3a4759" rx="2" />
            <text x="120" y="94" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">$484.00</text>
            <rect x="193" y="101" width="60" height="109" fill="#3a4759" rx="2" />
            <text x="223" y="94" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">$484.00</text>
            <rect x="297" y="50" width="60" height="160" fill="#3a4759" rx="2" />
            <text x="327" y="43" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">$712.00</text>
            <rect x="400" y="50" width="60" height="160" fill="#3a4759" rx="2" />
            <text x="430" y="43" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">$712.00</text>
            <rect x="503" y="82" width="60" height="128" fill="#d97706" rx="2" />
            <text x="533" y="75" fill="#d97706" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">$568.80</text>
            <rect x="607" y="101" width="60" height="109" fill="#3a4759" rx="2" />
            <text x="637" y="94" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">$483.00</text>
            <rect x="710" y="101" width="60" height="109" fill="#3a4759" rx="2" />
            <text x="740" y="94" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">$483.00</text>

            <line x1="80" y1="101" x2="770" y2="101" stroke="#6bb0a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />

            <text x="120" y="228" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 20</text>
            <text x="223" y="228" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 21</text>
            <text x="327" y="228" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 22</text>
            <text x="430" y="228" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 23</text>
            <text x="533" y="228" fill="#d97706" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">Aug 24</text>
            <text x="637" y="228" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 25</text>
            <text x="740" y="228" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Aug 26</text>
            <text x="80" y="246" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11">Modeled from each day's advertised rate and promotion — analysis/promo_cost_model.py.</text>
            <text x="80" y="258" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="11">The 22nd and 23rd carry the earlier $1-first-month offer against the raised $237 rate.</text>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <!-- The Breakdown Table -->
        <div class="breakdown-grid">
          <div class="breakdown-card">
            <h4>What the page displayed on 24 August</h4>
            <div class="ad-mockup">
              <span class="ad-tag">Month 1–4 · 40% OFF</span>
              <div class="ad-price">
                <s class="ad-strike">$237 / mo</s>
                <strong class="ad-deal">$142.20 / mo</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="ad-claim">★ Total Estimated 12-Month Savings: <strong>$380</strong><br><small>Four months at 40% off the displayed reference rate is 4 × ($237 − $142.20) = $379.20; the page truncates it to $380.</small></div>
            </div>
            <p class="breakdown-note">
              The arithmetic is correct <em>only if you accept that the unit actually cost $237</em>. This panel is a transcription recorded during a live-page inspection on 24 August 2026 — the scraper schema did not retain the savings field, the page HTML, or a screenshot.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="breakdown-card breakdown-card--truth">
            <h4>What the daily record shows</h4>
            <div class="math-breakdown">
              <div class="math-row">
                <span>Reference rate on 20 and 25 August:</span>
                <strong>$161.00 / mo</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row">
                <span>Renter pays during the promotion window:</span>
                <strong>$142.20 / mo</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row highlight-delta">
                <span>Lower monthly payment, ($161.00 − $142.20) × 4:</span>
                <strong class="text-accent">$75.20</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row highlight-reference">
                <span>Difference between the two reference rates, ($237 − $161) × 4:</span>
                <strong class="text-alert">$304.00</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="math-row">
                <span>Four months at the 24 August offer vs the adjacent offers:</span>
                <strong class="text-alert">+$85.80</strong>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="breakdown-note">
              <strong>80.2% of the advertised savings figure rests on the elevated reference rate</strong> rather than on any change in what the unit cost on the days either side of it. No intent is attributed: the record shows a sequence and a cost, not a reason.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- VISUAL 3: The September 14 Trade & Shapley Decomposition -->
      <section class="visual-card">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <span class="visual-card__eyebrow">The September Unwind · Portfolio Modeling</span>
          <h2>The "Rate Cut" That Quietly Raised Consumer Costs</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            On September 14, headline rates fell across the portfolio — no announcement was made; the change was observed in the daily snapshot.
            Across 59,045 exact-matched modelable listings, rates fell 14.7%. 
            At the same time roughly half the promotional value was withdrawn, leaving modeled four-month cost on matched offers slightly <strong>higher</strong> than before.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="waterfall-container">
          <div class="waterfall-bars">
            <div class="wf-bar">
              <span class="wf-val down">−15.4%</span>
              <div class="wf-block wf-block--down" style="height: 110px;"></div>
              <span class="wf-label">Rate Cut Impact<br><small>Lower monthly rent</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-sign">+</div>
            <div class="wf-bar">
              <span class="wf-val up">+16.5%</span>
              <div class="wf-block wf-block--up" style="height: 118px;"></div>
              <span class="wf-label">Promo Slash Impact<br><small>Withdrawn discounts</small></span>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-sign">=</div>
            <div class="wf-bar wf-bar--result">
              <span class="wf-val up"><strong>+1.1%</strong></span>
              <div class="wf-block wf-block--result" style="height: 24px;"></div>
              <span class="wf-label"><strong>Net Customer Cost</strong><br><small>Modeled 4-month spend</small></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="wf-caption">
            <strong>Shapley decomposition of the 14 September reset:</strong> 
            Looking at headline rates alone describes a customer windfall. Looking at both fields together describes something else:
            the rate reduction and the promotional withdrawal are close to the same size, and they point in opposite directions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- VISUAL 4: Tested in Public — The Living Ledger & September 18 Walkback -->
      <section class="visual-card visual-card--ledger">
        <div class="visual-card__header">
          <div class="ledger-pill">LIVING LEDGER AUDIT · 18 SEPTEMBER 2026</div>
          <h2>The Reset Walkback: Caught Live 96 Hours Later</h2>
          <p class="visual-card__desc">
            Had our study frozen on September 14, it would have claimed Public Storage locked in a 25% lower rate regime entering Q4. 
            The daily pipeline stayed online. On <strong>18 September 2026</strong>, Public Storage logged an average price restoration of roughly +12% (panel mean; the median-of-ratios index returned to 0.9800), with 22,772 SKUs repriced (18,828 up, 3,944 down) and 17,935 promotions rewritten.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Matched Panel Index SVG -->
        <div class="panel-index-box">
          <div class="index-metric">
            <span class="index-metric__lbl">Matched Panel Index (13 Sept = 1.0000)</span>
            <span class="index-metric__num">0.9800</span>
            <span class="index-metric__sub">Only 2% below starting rate, not 25%</span>
          </div>

          <div class="index-timeline">
            <div class="tl-node">
              <span class="tl-date">13 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val">1.0000</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">Baseline</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
            <div class="tl-node tl-node--down">
              <span class="tl-date">14 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val text-alert">0.7667</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">Coordinated reset · 31,244 price events</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
            <div class="tl-node tl-node--sealed">
              <span class="tl-date">15 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val">0.7667</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">Predictions sealed · 74 price events</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
            <div class="tl-node tl-node--restored">
              <span class="tl-date">18 Sept</span>
              <strong class="tl-val text-accent">0.9800</strong>
              <span class="tl-status">+12% panel mean (22,772 repriced)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: The Sealed Predictions -->
      <section class="study-section">
        <h2>The Pre-Registered Prediction (Sealed 15 September 2026)</h2>
        <p>
          Public Storage reports Q3 in late October. The three predictions below were sealed in commit <code>2026-09-15-q3-prediction-and-ledger-gap.md</code> before results exist.
        </p>

        <div class="pred-grid">
          <div class="pred-item">
            <div class="pred-item__badge">P1 · Primary</div>
            <h3>Q3 Promotional Discounts Given</h3>
            <p>Q2 2026 reported promo discounts up 16.1% YoY. Following summer discounting and the September contraction:</p>
            <div class="pred-item__statement">
              <strong>P1:</strong> Q3 promotional discounts will still be up YoY, but growth rate will decelerate below +16.1%.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pred-item">
            <div class="pred-item__badge">P2 · Primary</div>
            <h3>Q3 New-Customer Contract Rates</h3>
            <p>Q2 reported new contract rates up 1.6% YoY (first positive reading since 2021). Weighting pre vs post reset days:</p>
            <div class="pred-item__statement">
              <strong>P2:</strong> Q3 new-customer contract rate growth will come in below +1.6% YoY.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pred-item pred-item--counter">
            <div class="pred-item__badge">P3 · Counter-Guidance Bet</div>
            <h3>Q4 New-Customer Contract Rates</h3>
            <p>Management guided move-in rents to positive low single digits. Our daily volatility and demand models indicate:</p>
            <div class="pred-item__statement">
              <strong>P3:</strong> Q4 new-customer contract rates will be flat or negative YoY, directly contradicting company guidance.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Dual Doors to the Full Engine -->
      <section class="doors-section">
        <div class="doors-header">
          <span class="doors-eyebrow">Inspect the Data & Tools</span>
          <h2>The Heavy Lifting Lives in the Live Engine</h2>
          <p class="doors-desc">
            This teardown summarizes the core findings. For the complete mathematical proofs, raw accounting tables, and national market coverage, dive straight into the rate monitor:
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doors-grid">
          <!-- Door 1: Case Study & Econometric Proof (#study) -->
          <div class="door-card door-card--study">
            <div class="door-card__top">
              <span class="door-badge door-badge--study">Econometric Proof</span>
              <span class="door-hash">#study</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Full Methodology & 59k-Offer Accounting</h3>
            <p class="door-text">
